<CourseLayout title="Recover the impossible." description="Operation Last Light. Four roles, six areas and the last intact research archive at Meridian Station." eyebrow="THE FINAL MISSION / MERIDIAN" wide>
<StudyRoutes assessment="final-project"/>
<section class="callout"><h2>Online final mission: Operation Last Light.</h2><p>Recover Meridian Station's archive using the skills from all twelve weeks. The demonstration below, <strong>Operation Lamplight</strong>, is a different worked example. Your playable Last Light trial begins beneath it.</p><ol><li><strong>Start or resume.</strong> For a first rehearsal, choose Baseline, select Start new trial and confirm if prompted. Then choose the Declared recovery objective before selecting a role or operating equipment. Saved work resumes automatically with its initial objective locked; start a new trial to choose a different objective.</li><li><strong>Preserve the plan and a revision.</strong> Before practical checks, the Coordinator records Version 1 at Dispatch. Return later to record an explained revision, keeping the original.</li><li><strong>Choose the relevant checks.</strong> Read the current source and custody conditions, then investigate the dependencies of your selected objective. Physical recovery needs support and transport; digital recovery needs transmission authority, power and receipt; stabilisation needs continuing support and a monitoring handover. The journal gives optional control help; choose your investigation order and justify omitted checks. Solo practice lets you switch roles; teams share one browser and rotate control.</li><li><strong>Finish and keep the record.</strong> Complete your objective’s required conditions, perform the selected intervention and receiving handover, then record the evidence for physical custody, digital receipt or stable handover at Dispatch. Resolve that outcome, read the debrief and export. Write the team explanation after playing.</li></ol><p><a href={withBase("/assessments/final-project/")}>Read the full final-project steps and submission checklist →</a></p></section>
<DemonstrationLink id="assessment-final"/>
<Mission kind="recovery"/>
</CourseLayout>
